B.ak8=new A.hA("1. Introduction",'ClassRealm ("we," "our," or "the System") is committed to protecting the privacy, confidentiality, and security of personal and academic information of all students, parents/guardians, teachers, and administrators at Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we process and store it, and how users may exercise their rights\u2014including account and data deletion\u2014in strict compliance with Republic Act No. 10173, otherwise known as the Data Privacy Act of 2012, and its Implementing Rules and Regulations.')
B.akg=new A.hA("2. Information We Collect","We collect only the minimum personal, academic, and technical data necessary to deliver academic management services:\n\u2022 Students: Full Name, Learner Reference Number (LRN), School/Personal Email Address, Date of Birth, Gender, Grade Level, and Section.\n\u2022 Parents/Guardians: Full Name, Email Address, Contact/Mobile Number, Relationship to the linked student(s), and linked Student LRN(s).\n\u2022 Teachers & Administrators: Full Name, Email Address, Contact Number, Subject Specialization, Consultation Hours, and optional public directory links.\n\u2022 RFID and Attendance Data: Assigned RFID Card Unique Identifier (UID), daily time-in/time-out scan timestamps, attendance status (Present, Late, Absent, Excused), and scanner device logs captured via classroom ESP32 RFID readers or teacher NFC devices.\n\u2022 Academic and Classwork Data: Written Works (WW), Performance Tasks (PT), Quarterly Examination (EX) scores, uploaded activity submissions/files, computed initial and transmuted grades (Strengthened Senior High School Curriculum under DepEd Order No. 15, s. 2026), and teacher feedback.\n\u2022 Assessment Integrity Telemetry: During active online quizzes and exams only, the System logs app lifecycle changes (tab switches, window minimize/focus loss, and copy attempts) to uphold examination integrity. ClassRealm does NOT record camera video, microphone audio, personal photos, contacts, or GPS location.\n\u2022 Device Security Metadata: Anonymous device installation identifiers, login timestamps, and failed authentication counters used solely to prevent brute-force attacks and unauthorized account access.")
B.ak3=new A.hA("3. How We Use Your Information","Your data is processed strictly for legitimate educational and institutional purposes:\n\u2022 Authenticating user identity and providing role-based access to the Admin, Teacher, Student, and Parent portals;\n\u2022 Recording, computing, and reporting daily attendance (including DepEd School Form 2 exports) and quarterly academic grades;\n\u2022 Delivering real-time attendance, grade, and school broadcast notifications to students and linked parents/guardians;\n\u2022 Sending One-Time Passwords (OTPs), account verification codes, and security alerts via email;\n\u2022 Maintaining examination integrity during digital assessments and auditing system security.\nWe do NOT sell, rent, trade, or use student or parent personal data for commercial advertising or third-party marketing.")
B.ak_=new A.hA("4. Offline-First Local Storage and Cloud Synchronization","ClassRealm operates on an offline-first architecture using a local SQLite (Drift) database on your device paired with secure cloud synchronization. When you use the app offline, academic and attendance records are cached locally on your device and automatically transmitted over encrypted HTTPS/TLS connections to our cloud database once internet connectivity is restored. Logging out of your account clears active session tokens on the device.")
B.akb=new A.hA("5. Third-Party Infrastructure and Service Providers","To ensure enterprise-grade reliability and security, ClassRealm utilizes trusted cloud service providers that process data strictly on our behalf:\n\u2022 Google Firebase Authentication: For secure password authentication, session token management, and account security.\n\u2022 Supabase (PostgreSQL Cloud Database & Storage): For encrypted cloud storage of academic records, attendance logs, and learning materials with Row-Level Security (RLS).\n\u2022 Google Gemini AI (Teacher Portal Only): Used by teachers to assist in generating DepEd-aligned lesson plan drafts. Student personal identities (names, LRNs, emails) are never sent to AI models.")
B.akc=new A.hA("6. Data Sharing, Visibility, and 18+ Student Privacy Rights",'\u2022 Access to student data is strictly restricted to the student, their assigned subject teachers, class adviser, authorized school administrators, and verified linked parents/guardians.\n\u2022 Under RA 10173, students aged 18 and above may restrict parent/guardian visibility of their Term Grades and Final Grades through the "Parent / Guardian Privacy Controls" in Student Settings.')
B.akd=new A.hA("7. Data Security Measures","We implement organizational, physical, and technical security measures including HTTPS/TLS encryption in transit, salted password hashing, Row-Level Security (RLS) database policies, role-based access controls, OTP verification for sensitive actions, and progressive rate-limiting against unauthorized login attempts.")
B.ak1=new A.hA("8. Data Retention Policy","Personal and academic records are retained only for the duration of the active Academic School Year and the retention period required by Department of Education (DepEd) school record-keeping guidelines. Inactive or graduated accounts are archived and purged in accordance with school administration schedules.")
B.ak4=new A.hA("9. Account and Data Deletion Policy (Google Play & RA 10173 Compliance)",'Users (Students, Parents/Guardians, and Teachers) have the right to request the deletion of their ClassRealm user account and associated personal data at any time:\n\u2022 In-School Request: Submit a request directly to your Class Adviser (for Students and Parents) or the School System Administrator at Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School.\n\u2022 Email Request: Send an email with the subject line "ClassRealm Account Deletion Request" to the ClassRealm System Administrator / Support Team using your registered email address, stating your Full Name, User Role (Student/Parent/Teacher), and registered Email or LRN.\n\u2022 Verification & Timeline: To protect against unauthorized deletion, the Administrator or Adviser will verify the requester\'s identity and process the account deletion within seven (7) to fourteen (14) school days.\n\u2022 Deleted vs. Retained Records: Upon approval, your Firebase Authentication credentials, login profile, device tokens, and personal portal access are permanently deleted. Official academic grades and attendance records required by the Department of Education (DepEd) as part of official school registries remain under the custody of Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School until the end of the mandatory DepEd retention period.')
B.ak2=new A.hA("10. Your Rights Under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173)","As a data subject under Philippine law, you have the right to be informed, the right to access your personal data, the right to object, the right to rectification of inaccurate records, the right to erasure or blocking, and the right to data portability.")
B.aka=new A.hA("11. Contact Information","For privacy inquiries, data correction requests, or account deletion requests, please coordinate with:\n\u2022 Data Protection / System Administrator: ClassRealm Capstone Team & School Administration\n\u2022 Institution: Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School (Calamba City, Laguna)\n\u2022 Contact Channel: Your Class Adviser, School ICT Coordinator, or the official ClassRealm Administrator office at Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School.")
